ntime and the actual scoped SQLite, Tcl, readline, Berkeley DB, Ruby/documentation, and limited libintl/PCRE2 results without converting them into full provider or distribution admission.\n- Keep the live `.long`/`.word` TLS overwrite hazard prominent. The guard proposal is published in #11 but not applied to the runtime repository.\n- Record #12's source/image/parent/generation-bound exit contracts and two-sided negative control, preserving raw DWORDs without a normalization shim.\n- Record the confirmed `!ccache`/missing-Texinfo cause, refuted symlink/cache hypotheses, and published fix `a0b773d`; actual binutils CI remains pending at the cited receipt snapshot.\n- Preserve crutkas/msys2-runtime#33's transient pacman mirror failure alongside its green same-head rerun.\n\n## Evidence and limitations\n\nExplicit receipt scope flags govern over prose summaries. Producer-reported Tcl/coreutils/BDB/readline counts are labeled rather than presented as independently rerun suites. The absent V10 `verdict.json` remains secondhand history through the original inbox line 16. No frozen JSON/evidence, runtime source, provider payload, or release authority is changed.\n\nThe original historical narratives are preserved, including the false claim and later correction. Only `plan.md`, `inbox.md`, `status.md`, and their three `SHA256SUMS` entries change. All 75 continuity checksum entries match. Existing unrelated Ruby work remains uncommitted and excluded.","created_at":"2026-09-11T07:00:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T07:01:01Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ed4f015829947878ec1bc745ca56523e8643212d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/15/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm64-build/pulls/15/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/crutkas/msys2-woarm6